@node dokgen_cli
@section (dokgen cli)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines the command-line interface of the @command{dokgen}
program.  See the @ref{CLI} section for additional information.

The variable @code{spec} is the specification of the interface, a
@code{<configuration>} record as defined by the guile-config library.  It
names the program, states its version, license and author, and declares
the @code{api} subcommand with its @code{sources} argument and its
@code{destination} keyword.  The procedure @code{call} dispatches a
command line to the procedure that carries it out.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_cli_call}
@deffn Procedure call command spec
Call an appropriate procedure for the given command.

@strong{command} (list): A list of strings that represent a command-line
instruction passed to the program (see Guile's command-line procedure).

@strong{spec} (Configuration): A @code{<configuration>} record as
defined by the guile-config library, which specifies the command-line
interface of the program.

@strong{Result}: The @var{command} is followed.  If the command is not
recognized, display help information.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_cli_spec}
@defvar spec
This is a record of the type @code{<configuration>}, which has the
following fields:

@itemize 
@item
@code{name}
@item
