@node dokgen_commands
@section (dokgen commands)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures that are associated to every command
provided by the command-line interface of the @command{dokgen} program.
See the @ref{CLI} and @xref{dokgen_cli,(dokgen cli)} sections for
additional information.

The variable @code{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is the directory where the API
documentation is saved when the user does not choose one; its value is
@samp{doc/api}.  The documentation is written to a file named
@file{index.texi} inside that directory, and the images of the mermaid
diagrams it holds go in a @file{diagrams} directory beside it.

The procedure @code{api} writes that documentation; @code{check} only
reads, and says which of the exported names are documented nowhere.

@image{diagrams/dokgen_commands-cec3eac2,,,Mermaid diagram}


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_api}
@deffn Procedure api sources OPT: destination mermaid-command
Extract the API documentation of the given set of Guile Scheme modules.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Guile
Scheme modules that compose the code whose API documentation will be
extracted.  These paths can lead to both Scheme files or Scheme
directories.  For example:

@example 
(list «myproject/liby.scm»
      «myproject/liby»
      «myproject/libz.scm»
      «myproject/libz»)
@end example

@strong{destination} (string): Optional path to a directory where the
final Texinfo files will be saved.  If not provided,
@var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is used (see the module @ref{dokgen_commands}).
The diagrams the documentation holds are saved to a @file{diagrams}
directory inside it.

@strong{mermaid-command} (string): Optional command that draws a mermaid
diagram, with @code{%i} standing for the diagram's source and @code{%o}
for the path to write its image to.  An empty command draws nothing and
uses the diagrams already in the destination.

@strong{Result}: The API documentation is saved to the @var{destination}
directory.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_check}
@deffn Procedure check sources
Report the exported names the modules in SOURCES leave undocumented.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Scheme
files and directories, as for @code{api}.

@strong{Return value} (integer): The number of names reported, so that
the caller decides what an undocumented name means for the exit status.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_DEFAULT_DOC_PATH}
@defvr Variable DEFAULT_DOC_PATH
@verbatim 
"doc/api"
@end verbatim

@end defvr


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

