@node dokgen_data
@section (dokgen data)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures to retrieve data from Guile Scheme
libraries (e.g.  the names and attributes of their Scheme modules and
the objects these modules export).  This data is then passed to template
procedures to render API documentation in different formats.  See, for
example, the templates used to work with the
@uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo/,Texinfo format}:
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi,(dokgen templates stexi)}.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_api-symbols}
@deffn Procedure api-symbols interface
Return the symbols provided by the interface.

@strong{interface} (interface): A module's @code{<interface>} record as
returned by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (list of symbols): Where every symbol identifies a
public object exported by the @var{interface}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_file-path->module-name}
@deffn Procedure file-path->module-name file-path lib-parent-path
Convert the given Scheme file path into a module name.

@strong{file-path} (string): Absolute path to Guile Scheme module file.
For example: @samp{/home/user/project-x/libx/module-a.scm}.

@strong{lib-parent-path} (string): Absolute path to the directory
containing the library @var{file-path} belongs to.  For example:
@samp{/home/user/project-x/}.

@strong{Return value} (symbol): The name of the module.  For example:
@code{(libx module-a)}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_get-file-paths}
@deffn Procedure get-file-paths directory
Return a list of paths to Scheme files stored in the directory.

Scheme files are identified by their @code{.scm} extension.

@strong{directory} (string): Absolute path to a directory containing a
Guile Scheme library.

@strong{Return value} (list of strings): A list where every element
represents a path to a Scheme file.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_group-api-objects}
@deffn Procedure group-api-objects interface
Return the API objects grouped by kind.

A kind can be one of the following: macros, parameters, procedures,
record types, variables.

@strong{interface} (interface): An @code{<interface>} record as returned
by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (alist): Association list where every entry
corresponds to a kind of object and a list of its members.  Only groups
with members are returned.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_record-field}
@deffn Procedure record-field record field
Get the value of @var{field} from @var{record}.

@strong{record} (Guile record or SRFI 9 record): A record of any type.

@strong{field} (symbol): The name of the field.

@strong{Return value} (anything): The value of the field.

If the FIELD does not exist, a @var{no-such-field} exception is raised.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_undocumented-symbols}
@deffn Procedure undocumented-symbols interface
Return the names @var{interface} exports without documenting them.

@strong{interface} (interface): A module's @code{<interface>} record, as
returned by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (list of symbols): The documented gaps of the
module's API, in the order a reader meets them in the manual, so that a
build can fail on them.  An export that is bound to nothing is left out:
that name is a bug in the module and not a gap in its documentation, and
the @code{api} command is where it is reported.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

